  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "vo_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -324
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Voronoi Editor\n\nDrag the white handles to reshape the cells. Click empty space to add a point; X removes the one nearest the mouse. Hold L to relax the points (each slides towards the middle of its cell, and the mosaic evens out). D shows the Delaunay triangles, H the convex hull; R (or Reset) starts over.\n\nHow it works: the points are a State*. Each frame an Expression measures every point's distance to the mouse, Statistics (min) and Lookup (index-of) find the nearest, and a State remembers which one a press grabbed until release. The edit chain then moves, relaxes (Scatter's relax mode as a target), appends or removes points, and Cells draws Voronoi, Delaunay and hull from the result.",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 260
      }
    },
